%% VorDB KvCluster — 3-vnode system block for model checking and chaos simulation.
%%
%% Run model checker: make verify-check   (concatenates kv_store.vor + this file)
%% Run chaos sim:     make verify-chaos   (full-stack: RocksDB + ETS started first)
%%
%% READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING A GREEN RESULT — see docs/VERIFICATION_AUDIT_2026-08.md.
%%
%% The `connect` edges below are DECORATIVE at the model-checking tier. KvStore
%% contains no `send` and no `broadcast`: every inter-vnode message VorDB
%% actually exchanges (lww_sync / set_sync / counter_sync) is produced by
%% `Erlang.vordb_ffi.gossip_send_vnode_deltas`, an extern, from the `every`
%% timer. The explorer does not model externs, so no agent ever puts a message
%% on the wire and the topology carries nothing. `mix vor.check` explores
%% exactly ONE state at depth 0 (F-004). Replication is not verified here.
%%
%% All three state fields are maps, and the explorer abstracts map operations to
%% `:unknown` (Vor KNOWN_ISSUES §5), so CRDT content is invisible to the checker
%% regardless. What survives is only what these sentinel invariants say.

system KvCluster do
  agent :v1, KvStore(node_id: :node1, vnode_id: 0, sync_interval_ms: 5000)
  agent :v2, KvStore(node_id: :node2, vnode_id: 1, sync_interval_ms: 5000)
  agent :v3, KvStore(node_id: :node3, vnode_id: 2, sync_interval_ms: 5000)

  connect :v1 -> :v2
  connect :v1 -> :v3
  connect :v2 -> :v1
  connect :v2 -> :v3
  connect :v3 -> :v1
  connect :v3 -> :v2

  %% Sentinel invariants: a store field never holds the bare atom `:error`.
  %%
  %% Named for what they actually test. They do NOT assert "is a map" — a store
  %% holding an extern-error tuple, a stale map, or a divergent map satisfies
  %% all three. Demonstrated: a chaos run with no VorDB infrastructure on the
  %% code path leaves every store as `{:vor_extern_error, ...}` and these still
  %% report PASS / substantive (F-006).
  %%
  %% `for_all` is reported `substantive` by construction — Vor's relevance axis
  %% treats a universal quantifier's subject as its (non-empty) domain, so a
  %% `for_all` invariant can never be flagged vacuous (GAP-016). The green badge
  %% on these three is not evidence that the check engaged with anything.
  safety "lww_store never becomes the :error sentinel" proven do
    for_all agents, lww_store != :error
  end

  safety "set_store never becomes the :error sentinel" proven do
    for_all agents, set_store != :error
  end

  safety "counter_store never becomes the :error sentinel" proven do
    for_all agents, counter_store != :error
  end

  %% Downgraded proven -> checked on 2026-08-09 (F-002).
  %%
  %% The current toolchain refuses these at `proven`: VACUOUS PROOF — the
  %% subject `v1.lww_store == :error` is never true in any explored state, so
  %% the implication holds by an empty antecedent. It was equally vacuous under
  %% the old toolchain; the old toolchain just did not say so.
  %%
  %% `checked` is the routing the refusal recommends. These are kept as a record
  %% of the shape, not as evidence. The comment they used to carry — that they
  %% detect cross-replica divergence — was false: they only ever compared
  %% against the `:error` atom, never against each other's contents.
  safety "v1 and v2 lww_store don't diverge to error" checked do
    never(v1.lww_store == :error and v2.lww_store != :error)
  end

  safety "v2 and v3 lww_store don't diverge to error" checked do
    never(v2.lww_store == :error and v3.lww_store != :error)
  end

  %% NOT DECLARED: a real convergence invariant (`never(v1.lww_store !=
  %% v2.lww_store)`). At the checker tier it is unexpressible in practice (both
  %% sides abstract to `:unknown`, so it is trivially true and would be flagged
  %% vacuous). At the simulation tier it would be red on every run, because the
  %% simulator has no anti-entropy: gossip goes through an extern to peers that
  %% do not exist in the harness. See F-007.
end
